-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- self-adjointness: the check of the whole construction
-- The invariant inner product of the Bargmann realisation: ⟨z^k, z^l⟩ = δ_kl k!(2j−k)!/(2j)! for each variable, so
-- a monomial's weight is the product of those. Q_v is self-adjoint and S = Σ ε q_IJK anti-self-adjoint (each q_IJK is
-- the commutator of two self-adjoint J_IJ²); R P_x E is self-adjoint for each root x (R = E†/s); and
-- tr(M_e M_e′)† = tr(M_e′ M_e). With G the Gram matrix of the vertex's kernel basis these read G S = −(G S)ᵀ,
-- G C_p = (G C_p)ᵀ, and G D^{(e,e′)}_pq = (G D^{(e′,e)}_qp)ᵀ branch by branch: identities among rational matrices
-- that hold only if the realisation, the holonomy maps, F̃ and the ε contraction are all right.
poly-head-nat : List Nat → Nat
poly-head-nat s = case s of
  nil → zero
  cons x rest → x
